---
  Agent Role Templates
  Create and inspect role profiles used by spawn_agent.agent_type.
  User templates live in $CODEX_HOME/agents/*.toml.
  Runtime tool catalog: open from a loaded thread to inspect current native tool ids.

  1. Create new template                 Edit a native TOML role draft for future sub-agent spawns
  2. Create template from current model  Seed a native TOML role draft with current model defaults
› 3. [user active] explorer              Role: explorer
                                         Source: user
                                         Status: active
                                         Overrides built-in role with the same name.
                                         Description: Custom explorer role for codebase discovery.
                                         Config file: $CODEX_HOME/agents/
                                         explorer.toml
                                         Config origin: $CODEX_HOME/agents
                                         Native profile fields: name, description,
                                         nickname_candidates, developer_instructions, model,
                                         model_provider, model_reasoning_effort, service_tier
                                         Declaration fields: description, config_file,
                                         nickname_candidates
                                         TOML fields: name, description, nickname_candidates,
                                         developer_instructions, model, model_provider,
                                         model_reasoning_effort, approval_policy,
                                         default_permissions, permissions, mcp_servers, hooks,
                                         tool_selection.allowed_tools, skills.config, apps
                                         Field sources: description=role-file metadata,
                                         config_file=$CODEX_HOME/agents discovery,
                                         nickname_candidates=role-file metadata,
                                         approval_policy=effective role file, apps=effective role
                                         file, default_permissions=effective role file,
                                         developer_instructions=effective role file,
                                         hooks=effective role file, mcp_servers=effective role
                                         file, model=effective role file, model_provider=effective
                                         role file, model_reasoning_effort=effective role file,
                                         name=role-file metadata, permissions=effective role file,
                                         skills.config=effective role file,
                                         tool_selection.allowed_tools=effective role file
                                         Validation: valid native TOML role file
                                         Nicknames: Ada
                                         Runtime use: no known threads with this agent_type in
                                         current TUI session
                                         Tool selection state: runtime allowlist; unmatched
                                         entries warn during tool planning and grant no access
                                         Runtime catalog reference: unavailable because no loaded
                                         thread was available for app-server catalog read.
                                         Template sets: model=gpt-5.3-codex,
                                         model_provider=deepseek, reasoning=high,
                                         developer_instructions, tool_selection=update_plan,
                                         codex_app/lookup
                                         Security sets: approval_policy=on-request,
                                         default_permissions=:read-only, permissions=1 profiles
                                         Subsystem sets: mcp_servers=1, hooks=1 handlers, skills=1
                                         config, apps=1 apps, apps_default
                                         Runtime binding: spawn_agent.agent_type `explorer`
                                         Enter: open template file for editing
                                         Availability: loaded threads use this TOML file after
                                         native config reload or restart; the TUI wizard triggers
                                         reload after successful create.
                                         Use: ask Codex to spawn a sub-agent with agent_type
                                         `explorer`.
  4. [built-in active] default           Default agent.
  5. [built-in shadowed] explorer        Use `explorer` for specific codebase questions.
  6. [built-in active] worker            Use for execution and production work.

  Press enter to confirm or esc to go back
